{{also|Wieder|wieder-}}
==Bavarian==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|bar|gem-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|bar|gmh|wider}}, from {{inh|bar|goh|widar||against}}, from {{inh|bar|gmw-pro|*wiþr||toward, against}}. Cognates include {{cog|de|wieder}} and {{cog|yi|ווידער}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|bar|/ˈvid̥ɐ/}}
* {{hyph|bar|wie|der}}

===Adverb===
{{head|bar|adverb}}

# [[again]]
#* {{quote-text|bar|title=Wien wörtlich|section=Impression im März|author=Josef Weinheber|year=1938|text=Wårme Sunn, dås erste Pråterveigerl:<br /> Ållweil '''wieder''' gfreust di wiara Kind.|t=Warm sun, the first violet:<br /> You always rejoice like a child '''again'''.}}

===References===
* {{R:bar:Hornung:2002|wida}}

==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|wider}}, whence {{cog|en|widdershins}} via {{cog|gml|-}} borrowing; from {{inh|de|goh|widar}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*wiþr||toward, against}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|wither}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈviːdɐ/|aa=standard}}
** {{audio|de|De-at-wieder.ogg|a=Austria}}
** {{audio|de|De-wieder.ogg}}
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvɪdɐ/|aa=regional,including western Germany,chiefly colloquial}}
* {{homophones|de|wider}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[again]]; {{n-g|indicates that the action taking place has happened before}}
#: {{ux|de|Siehst du, jetzt hast du’s schon '''wieder''' gesagt!|See, now you’ve said it '''again!'''}}
# [[back]]; {{n-g|indicates that the action will return something to its original state or position}}
#: {{ux|de|Schalte das Licht '''wieder''' aus.|Turn the light '''back''' off.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|de|hin und wieder}}
* {{l|de|immer wieder}}

